{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2159-04-26 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I understand you came in with right leg pain and ulcers. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2159-04-26 19:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started about three weeks ago. My right leg has been really tender, and I noticed an ulcer on the inside. Now there’s another one higher up. My nephrologist told me to come in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2159-04-26 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’re on dialysis, correct? And you’ve been keeping up with your sessions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2159-04-26 19:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I haven’t missed any. I’ve also been careful with my diet—no high phosphate foods."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2159-04-26 19:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ve checked your labs, and your potassium is very high—9.9—and your calcium and phosphate are also elevated. This, along with your history, makes us concerned about calciphylaxis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2159-04-26 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve heard of that. It’s related to calcium building up in the blood vessels, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2159-04-26 19:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And your PTH level is extremely high—1403—so your parathyroid glands are overactive, which is making this worse. We’ll start treatment with dialysis and medications to lower calcium and phosphate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2159-04-26 19:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need surgery for the parathyroid?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2159-04-26 19:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re considering it. High PTH is fueling the calciphylaxis. Removing the overactive glands may help. We’ll discuss it more after we stabilize you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2159-04-28 10:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a CT angiogram today. It shows severe calcification in your leg arteries, especially on the right. There’s a high-grade blockage in the superficial femoral artery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2159-04-28 10:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why my foot is so cold and dusky?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2159-04-28 10:47:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, poor blood flow is contributing. We’re worried about ischemia. We’ll need vascular surgery to open up those arteries."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2159-04-30 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had the parathyroidectomy this morning. All four glands were overactive. Your PTH dropped to 39—that’s a great sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2159-04-30 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2159-04-30 14:01:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but now we have a new concern—your calcium is dropping. Your bones are ‘hungry’ after years of high PTH, so they’re pulling calcium from your blood. We’ll need to monitor and replace it carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2159-04-30 14:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need IV calcium?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2159-04-30 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll give IV calcium gluconate and also increase calcium in your dialysis baths. We’ll check your ionized calcium every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2159-05-02 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ionized calcium is 0.92—quite low. We’re giving 4 grams of IV calcium gluconate now. We’ll keep a close eye on this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2159-05-02 08:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2159-05-02 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be if not managed. Low calcium can cause muscle cramps or heart issues. But we’re on top of it. You’re also on calcitriol and calcium pills to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2159-05-04 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You just came back from the procedure. We did an angioplasty and stenting on your right iliac and femoral arteries. We also did an atherectomy to remove plaque."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2159-05-04 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Did it help the blood flow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2159-05-04 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partially. Unfortunately, some plaque broke off and went downstream, blocking smaller vessels in your foot. Your foot is still poorly perfused."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2159-05-04 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the pain might not get better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2159-05-04 15:03:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting you on heparin, Plavix, and aspirin to prevent more clots. But yes, the pain is still significant. We’ll adjust your pain meds and may involve the pain service."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2159-05-05 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We had to take you back for another procedure. There was a pseudoaneurysm in your left groin and more blockages. We placed three stents and gave tPA to dissolve clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2159-05-05 07:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the blood flow better now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2159-05-05 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We restored some flow, but your foot is still cool and dusky. The vascular team will wait to see how much tissue demarcates before deciding if you need a below-knee amputation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2159-05-05 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s scary to hear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2159-05-05 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But we’re doing everything to save your limb. The good news is your calciphylaxis lesions are responding to intralesional sodium thiosulfate injections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2159-05-05 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The ones they gave me yesterday? They did feel a little better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2159-05-05 07:05:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, dermatology will continue those as outpatient. We stopped IV sodium thiosulfate because it was lowering your calcium too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2159-05-07 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ionized calcium is now 1.11—much better. We’re reducing the IV calcium but will keep monitoring daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2159-05-07 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2159-05-07 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. Your foot still needs close monitoring, and we need your INR stable. You’re back on warfarin after surgery—goal is 2.5 to 3.5 because of your mechanical valve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2159-05-07 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember—my valve needs strong anticoagulation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2159-05-07 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your INR was 3.4 this morning—perfect. We’ll keep it there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2159-05-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a skin biopsy. It confirmed calciphylaxis—calcium deposits in small blood vessels, no infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2159-05-09 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2159-05-09 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s a vascular calcification issue. That’s why we’re focusing on calcium balance and wound care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2159-05-11 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your foot isn’t improving much. Vascular surgery still wants to wait and see how much tissue becomes non-viable before deciding on amputation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2159-05-11 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared of losing my leg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2159-05-11 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. But rushing to amputation isn’t always best. We want to preserve as much limb as possible. Your pain is better with the new meds, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2159-05-11 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the OxyContin and Dilaudid help a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2159-05-11 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep that regimen. Pain worsening could mean more ischemia, so we’ll watch closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2159-05-14 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We placed a PICC line today so we can give IV meds safely. We also did another biopsy to confirm the calciphylaxis diagnosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2159-05-14 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the PICC for the calcium?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2159-05-14 11:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly, and for antibiotics if needed. Your MRSA screen was negative, so no infection there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2159-05-16 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. Hemoglobin is 8.2—we gave one unit of blood earlier when you were fatigued. You’re on Epogen during dialysis to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2159-05-16 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do feel less tired now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2159-05-16 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. Your dialysis is helping clear toxins and balance electrolytes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2159-05-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge soon. You’ll go to extended care for wound care and IV calcium support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2159-05-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I still need IV calcium?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2159-05-18 09:01:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, daily checks. If ionized calcium drops below 1.1, you’ll get IV calcium. It may take weeks for your bones to stop being ‘hungry.’"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2159-05-18 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my leg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2159-05-18 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Vascular surgery will see you as outpatient to decide on amputation. Dermatology will continue the sodium thiosulfate injections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2159-05-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your wound care will involve daily Xeroform dressings. Keep the area clean and avoid trauma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2159-05-20 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2159-05-20 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll stay on OxyContin 30mg twice daily, Dilaudid for breakthrough pain, and gabapentin. If pain worsens suddenly, call vascular surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2159-05-22 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day. You’re being discharged to extended care. Keep monitoring your weight—call if it goes up more than 3 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2159-05-22 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for everything. I’m nervous but ready to move forward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2159-05-22 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been through a lot, but you’re on the right path. Follow up with nephrology, vascular, and dermatology. We’ll be checking on you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2159-05-22 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2159-05-22 11:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. You’re strong, and we’re here for you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2159-04-26 18:55:00",
    "admission_end": "2159-05-22 19:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis was admitted for worsening right leg pain and ulcers, found to be due to calciphylaxis and severe peripheral arterial disease. She had markedly elevated PTH, leading to a parathyroidectomy, after which she developed hungry bone syndrome with symptomatic hypocalcemia requiring IV calcium replacement and close monitoring. A CT angiogram revealed critical stenosis in the right femoral artery, prompting angioplasty and stenting, complicated by distal embolization and persistent foot ischemia. Despite interventions, her right foot remained cool, dusky, and painful, with vascular surgery deferring amputation pending demarcation. Calciphylaxis lesions were managed with intralesional sodium thiosulfate after IV therapy was halted due to worsening hypocalcemia. Pain was controlled with a multimodal regimen, and anticoagulation was optimized for her mechanical valve. She was discharged to extended care with plans for ongoing wound care, calcium monitoring, and outpatient follow-up with vascular and dermatology teams.",
    "problems": [
      "Other disorders of calcium metabolism",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Peripheral arterial disease s/p angiography with atherectomy",
      "Post-parathyroidectomy hungry bone syndrome",
      "Calciphylaxis",
      "Anemia in chronic kidney disease",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Heart valve replaced by other means",
      "Aortic valve disorders",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Secondary hyperparathyroidism (of renal origin)",
      "Ulcer of calf",
      "Ulcer of lower limb, unspecified",
      "Hypoparathyroidism",
      "Embolism and thrombosis of other specified artery"
    ]
  }
}
